{"type":"npc","name":"Chionad","folder":"WtzfbkwXcJMUjIoF","system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":120,"temp":0,"max":120,"details":""},"ac":{"value":27,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":50}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"cold","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":10,"exceptions":[]},{"type":"fire","value":10,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","cryan","fey","luxan"],"details":"Speak with animals"},"level":{"value":8},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Chionads, also known as aurora nymphs, are spirits of the far north, of freezing winds, and of the lights that dance above boreal mountains. Although chionads live isolated lives on snowy peaks, they are playful and friendly spirits, taking joy in shaping snow and ice into delicate artwork and sculptures that glisten in the northern lights. They sing mysterious, echoing songs that carry through the chilly air for all to hear. Those who travel in the mountains with good intent know they are safe if they hear the song or see the light of a chionad, for chionads are protectors of those who become lost in the mountains or who have been attacked by the more violent denizens of the snowy heights.</p><hr /><p>Nymphs are embodiments and guardians of nature's most beautiful places, mystically bonded to their ward in a specific way. They often take the form of beautiful humanoids with vaguely elven features that match the aesthetics of their ward. Each subgroup of nymphs specializes in a different kind of ward, and chionads are no exception.</p><h2>Painting the Sky</h2><p>Chionads sometimes gather with their neighbors on nearby mountain peaks for an activity they call \"painting the sky.\" During these elaborate dances, multiple chionads work together to fill the firmament with vibrant, shifting colors. These displays most often resemble a typical (if especially glorious) aurora, though some arctic travelers have reported recognizable scenes amid the lights, such as recreations of epic battles or the coronation of fey monarchs from ages past.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 64/140/250 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Crafting, Diplomacy, Nature, Performance, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> air, body, bane, charisma, dexterity, energy resistant (cold, vitality), ice, intelligence, light, sensory (low-light vision), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.IihxWhRfpsBgQ5jS]{Enthrall}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.5esP2GVzvxWsMgaX]{Environmental Endurance}, @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.sf2e-spells.JCQxDEB0CFIoveu6]{Falling Icicles}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.IxhGEKl63R4QBvkj]{Frostbite}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.TTwOKGqmZeKSyNMH]{Gentle Landing}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.WBmvzNDfpwka3qT4]{Light}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.BBvV7qoXGdw09q1C]{Speak with Animals}, @UUID[Compendium.battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.sf2e-spells.FTjpdbJKibOcgZPN]{Winter's Grasp}), throwing, water, wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Brian Nowosatka","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":0},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":7}},"perception":{"details":"snow vision","mod":18,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":17,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":18},"crafting":{"base":16},"diplomacy":{"base":19},"nature":{"base":18},"performance":{"base":19},"survival":{"base":18}},"traits":{"value":["co